data.content:
## What Changed

Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi 10.0 upgrades to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2.x**, which targets **OpenAPI 3.1** (based on JSON Schema). Key breaking changes affecting your code:

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1.x) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2.x) |
|---|---|
| `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. | Replaced by `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` |
| `schema.Nullable = true` | Use `schema.Type = JsonSchemaType.Null \| otherType` |
| `new OpenApiSecurityRequirement { [scheme] = scopes }` | Dictionary syntax changed — use `OpenApiSecurityRequirement.SchemeRequirements` |
| `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` | `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` (same, but namespace moved) |
| `OpenApiResponse` in `Responses` dict | Now uses `OpenApiResponse` keyed in a `Dictionary<string, OpenApiResponse>` (similar) |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // OpenApiString is gone; use JsonNode instead
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses ??= new Dictionary<string, OpenApiResponse>();
    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    // Use OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference for inline references
    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");

    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // Nullable property removed; strip Null from the type flags
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

## Summary of Fixes

1. **`new OpenApiString("1.0")`** → `JsonValue.Create("1.0")` (add `using System.Text.Json.Nodes`)
2. **`new OpenApiSecurityScheme { Reference = ... }`** → `new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2")` (from `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References`)
3. **`property.Value.Nullable = false`** → `property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null` (OpenAPI 3.1 uses type arrays, not a nullable flag)
